'''Six Invitational''' is an annual professional Rainbow Six Siege tournament hosted by Ubisoft, the game's developer and publisher. Located in Montreal, home of the Ubisoft studio working on the game, the tournament gathers the best teams from all around the world. The event marks the end of previous year and acts as an informal World Cup.

==About==
===Format===


*'''Group Stage:''' ''February 7th - 11th, 2023''<ref name="event announced for 2023">{{cite web |url=https://www.ubisoft.com/en-us/esports/rainbow-six/siege/news-updates/7q7WS6oWtWNnW9wjvHWbQh/six-invitational-2023|title=SIX INVITATIONAL 2023 |publisher=Ubisoft |date=2022-11-28}}</ref>
**Four Round-Robin format groups
*** Each group has 5 teams
***All teams play each other once
***All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** {{Bgcolortext|seedup|1<sup>st</sup> placed team}} from each group advance to the '''Upper Bracket Round 2''' of the '''Playoffs'''.
** {{Bgcolortext|up|2<sup>nd</sup>-3<sup>rd</sup> placed teams}} from each group advance to the '''Upper Bracket Round 1''' of the '''Playoffs'''.
*** 2<sup>nd</sup> placed team in each group will pick their first opponent for the playoffs from the 3<sup>rd</sup> place finish from any group other than their own group.
*** The pick order will be determined by comparing the scores of all 2nd place finishers.
**{{Bgcolortext|down|Bottom team}} in each group is eliminated.
**{{Bgcolortext|stayup|Remaining teams}} advance to the '''Lower Bracket''' of the '''Playoffs'''.
**<span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for Scoring system''</span>
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="width:760px; margin-left:45px">
*4 points for a 2:0 win
*3 points for a 2:1 win
*1 point for a 1:2 loss
*0 points for a 0:2 loss </div>
**<span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker2" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker2" style="width:760px; margin-left:45px">
#Mini league points
#Mini league round difference
#Overall map difference
#Overall round difference
#Overall rounds won
#Rematch
*If at any point the number of tied teams is reduced or divided into several groups of tied teams, the tiebreaker will begin again with the teams that are still tied.</div>

*'''Playoffs:''' ''February 13th - 19th, 2023''<ref name="event announced for 2023"></ref>
**Double-Elimination bracket
**All matches (excl. Grand Final) are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
**Grand Final is {{Abbr/Bo5}}, with no map advantage.

